  "title": "Categorize the hand-typed shopping items the scorecard still misses",
  "description": "make shopping-list-categorizer-test (hand-typed prod items only) still misses these with the keyword rules on (10 mismatches, 14 Other, 12 of them labeled Other) and from the catalog alone (15 mismatches, 25 Other), after Open Food Facts names (ramekin-core/src/catalog/data/open_food_facts.json, 2026-10-20) placed Cheerios, Cheez its, Cereal, Oatmeal, Pretzels, Rice cakes, Ranch, Baked beans, S'mores, salad and whole-grain bread. \n\
- Typos: 'Banning soda' (baking soda), 'Cheers it's' (Cheez-Its), 'Calfia almond milk' (Califia). \n\
- Names neither the catalog nor Open Food Facts knows: 'Harissa', 'Lemon ginger tea', 'Ranch powder', 'Sandwich meat', 'Slaw', 'Oats stuff', 'Potato salad' (keyword rules make it Produce; labeled Other). \n\
- Extra words around a known name: 'ice cream bars or similar', 'mini microwave popcorns', 'whole-grain crackers'. \n\
- Open Food Facts aisles that disagree with the labels: 'Jello' -> Snacks (labeled Baking), 'Dip' -> Cheese (labeled Other). \
'Ground flaxseed' -> Nuts & Dried Fruit follows the catalog (labeled Baking; consider relabeling). \n\
Typos, dishes and unknown names are what the AI name resolver (server/src/ingredient_names.rs) is for, but it only returns a catalog key or a calorie estimate, and estimates carry no category (prod has harissa and slaw resolved as estimates, with no aisle). \
Having it return a shopping aisle with every answer, and queueing the live shopping items created before the resolver existed (prod has no rows for Jello, Cheerios or Pretzels), would cover these in prod. \
The offline scorecard runs without learned answers, so it won't show that.",
